\
**Basic**\
- **Object** \'97 a dot. Has no internal structure. Only its arrows matter.\
- **Morphism** \'97 an arrow `f: A \uc0\u8594  B` from one object to another.\
- **Composition** \'97 sticking two arrows end-to-end: `g \uc0\u8728  f`.\
- **Identity** \'97 a do-nothing arrow `id_A` for every object.\
- **Isomorphism** \'97 arrows `f: A \uc0\u8594  B` and `g: B \u8594  A` where `g \u8728  f = id_A` and `f \u8728  g = id_B`. A and B are "the same" in this category.\
\
**Functors**\
- **Functor** \'97 a map between categories that preserves composition and identity.\
- **Forgetful functor** \'97 strips structure (e.g., group \uc0\u8594  set).\
- **Free functor** \'97 adds structure generically (e.g., set \uc0\u8594  free group).\
\
**Natural Transformations**\
- **Natural transformation** \'97 a map between two functors. Says "these two constructions are systematically the same."\
\
**Universal Constructions**\
- **Product** `A \'d7 B` \'97 the most general object that maps to both A and B.\
- **Coproduct** `A + B` \'97 the most general object that receives maps from both A and B.\
- **Pullback** \'97 a product over a shared target. Gluing with compatibility.\
- **Pushout** \'97 a coproduct over a shared source. Forcing agreement.\
- **Limit** \'97 universal object that "sees" a whole diagram.\
- **Colimit** \'97 universal object that "glues" a whole diagram.\
\
**Adjunctions**\
- **Adjunction** `F \uc0\u8867  G` \'97 a pair of functors with `Hom(FA, B) \u8773  Hom(A, GB)`. Captures "free vs. forgetful," optimization, duality.\
\
**Higher Structure**\
- **Monad** `T` \'97 a functor with `unit` and `join`. Lets you compose effectful maps (probability, state, error).\
- **Comonad** \'97 dual of a monad. Spreads context outward.\
- **Monoidal category** \'97 a category with a tensor product `\uc0\u8855 ` and a unit object `I`. Where you can do `A \u8855  B` and reorder wires.\
- **Braided / Symmetric** \'97 monoidal with a swap map `A \uc0\u8855  B \u8773  B \u8855  A`.\
- **Closed category** \'97 has an "internal hom" `A \uc0\u8658  B`, an object representing morphisms. Cartesian closed categories = typed lambda calculus.\
- **2-category** \'97 categories where morphisms themselves have morphisms (natural transformations are 2-cells).\
- **Topos** \'97 a category that behaves like Set. Has logic, truth values, quantifiers. Generalized universe of mathematics.\
\
**Theorems**\
- **Yoneda lemma** \'97 an object is determined by its outgoing arrows. `Nat(Hom(\uc0\u8722 , A), F) \u8773  F(A)`.\
- **Adjoint functor theorem** \'97 conditions under which a functor has an adjoint.\
\
That is the full toolkit. Everything else is an application.\
